            <ArticleTitle>[Paroxysmal hemicrania preceding Pancoast's syndrome].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>151-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of Pancoast's syndrome whose first symptom was facial pain is reported. Pain was identical to chronic paroxysmal hemicrania described by Sjaastad and Dale in 1974. It seems to result from a lesion of the sympathetic nerves in the neck.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
